  "p_items": {
   "type": "array",
   "default": [
    {
     "p": "Barak Yahalom, DVM, is Chief Executive Officer and Chief Scientific Officer of Alpha Preclinical and a founding member of its scientific team. He sets the scientific direction for client programs at Alpha's Worcester, Massachusetts facility and works directly with sponsors on study design, from PK/PD and dose selection through efficacy in validated disease models."
    },
    {
     "p": "Barak has more than 20 years of scientific and veterinary experience in biotechnology and preclinical contract research. Before Alpha, he was director of in vivo pharmacology at several biotech companies and held positions of increasing responsibility at Boston Children's Hospital and Biomere. He earned his DVM at the Koret School of Veterinary Medicine and a BS in animal science, both at the Hebrew University of Jerusalem, and serves on the Sideromics Scientific Advisory Board."
    },
    {
     "p": "His eight peer-reviewed papers, published from 2004 to 2021, cover the kinds of work Alpha runs today: rat models of type 1 diabetes (<i>Diabetes</i>; <i>Comparative Medicine</i>), antidiabetic peptides in experimental diabetes (<i>Diabetologia</i>), mRNA liver depot therapy for hemophilia B and Fabry disease (<i>Gene Therapy</i>; <i>Molecular Therapy</i>), and pediatric anesthesia and analgesia models, including his first-authored model of spinal anesthesia in infant rats (<i>Anesthesiology</i>, 2011)."
    },
    {
     "p": "He is most interested in pairing a deep understanding of disease models with well-executed translational studies, so that a client's new science can become a therapy or device."
    }
   ]
  },
