  "p_items_2": {
   "type": "array",
   "default": [
    {
     "p": "Joan Flanagan, PhD, is President and Chief Operating Officer of Alpha Preclinical and a founding member of its scientific team. She runs Alpha's operations and leads its metabolic and autoimmune disease programs, guiding the development, execution and strategy of client studies."
    },
    {
     "p": "Joan has more than 20 years of experience in in vivo preclinical contract research, with positions of increasing responsibility at Biomedical Research Models and Charles River Laboratories. She earned her PhD in molecular biology and biochemistry at UMass Medical School in Worcester and her BS in biochemistry at UMass Amherst."
    },
    {
     "p": "Her publications trace that path from molecular biology to disease models. Her first-authored paper in <i>Nucleic Acids Research</i> (1999) and a 2003 paper in <i>Nature Structural Biology</i> examined the yeast SWI/SNF chromatin-remodeling complex. She then co-authored work characterizing rodent models of diabetes and metabolic disease: the BBZDR/Wor rat for the complications of type 2 diabetes (<i>ILAR Journal</i>, 2004), the LEW.1WR1 rat model of autoimmune diabetes (<i>Diabetes</i>, 2005) and the C57BL/6NCrl-lb mouse model of metabolic syndrome (<i>FASEB Journal</i> abstract, 2007)."
    },
    {
     "p": "She contributes to the region's research community through the Massachusetts Society for Medical Research, the New England Branch of AALAS and the Worcester Technical High School Scientific Advisory Board."
    }
   ]
